<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orgetorix</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 60 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orgetorix was a wealthy Helvetian noble who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, planned the migration of the Helvetii to western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and conspired with Casticus of the Sequani and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumnorix">Dumnorix</a> of the Aedui to seize royal power. Accused of aiming at kingship, he died, perhaps by suicide, before his trial in 60 BCE, but the Helvetii carried out the migration in 58 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orgetorix.jpg" alt="Orgetorix" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Łukasz &quot;Wanderer&quot; Grzeszczak at Polish Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orgetorix-coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
